\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {\mbox  {II-E}}Summary of the Reinforcement Twinning loop}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Reinforcement Twinning closed loop for an episode $n$, from policy deployment to the selection of the policy for episode $n+1$. (1) Following initialization with $\pi _{\mathrm  {BL}}$, an information-oriented or performance-oriented policy is deployed by supplying $\mathbf  x^\ast $ to the baseline feedback controller. (2) The physical episode is performed in the presence of exogenous inputs $\mathbf  z$, and observations $\mathbf  o_\bullet $ are acquired. (3) The episode record $\mathcal  E^{(n)}$ is stored in $\mathcal  B_n$ and the physical return $\mathcal  R_\bullet ^{(n)}$ is evaluated. (4) The episode is replayed in the DT from reconstructed initial conditions. During the information phase, including the initial baseline replay, $\boldsymbol  {\theta }_p$ is identified by comparing $\overline  {\mathbf  o}_\circ $ with $\mathbf  o_\bullet $. During the subsequent performance phase, $\boldsymbol  {\theta }_p$ is kept fixed and paired returns are obtained for surrogate calibration. (5) Candidate episodes are evaluated virtually to quantify their expected information or their DT return around $\pi _{\mathrm  {MB}}$. (6) For $e_{n+1}=1$, $\boldsymbol  {\theta }_\iota ^{(n+1)}$ is selected by minimizing $\mathcal  J_{\mathrm  {info}}$; for $e_{n+1}=0$, $\pi _{\mathrm  {MB}}$ and initial calibration policies are deployed first, after which further policies are selected using EI and the calibrated return transfer surrogate. In the adopted schedule, the information phase is completed first, after which the identified model is frozen during the performance phase.}}{7}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:rt_framework}{{1}{7}{}{figure.1}{}}
